Z||000000||DXR_DAD||08-09-2000||12:04 AM||||86-c-16 ?? Parking brake. What was the problem and what was done to fix it. Can you tell if it was done by looking at the brakes?<BR>Are there parts that are different? Just looking for some info on this. I don't have any adjustment AT ALL on the adjuster!<P><BR>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000001||2birds||08-09-2000||12:16 AM||||For Manual Transmissions only (don't know why).  Look at the pistons in your rear calipers.  If there is a plastic check valve in the center of the piston face (behind the pad), you are pre-recall.  The ones that have been fixed under the recall have solid center pistons installed, P/N 18019027, according to my dealer receipt.  My check valves started to leak, and after the dealer rebuilt the calipers, the right rear still dragged, and they ended up replacing the e-brakes cables too, all under the recall.  <BR>I think the e-brake cables were the meat of the recall, but the calipers were what started my problem.  I just wish I had known about the recall before I rebuilt them myself.  I don't know if the campaign is still open, but mine was done in 1995.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||08-09-2000||07:31 PM||||Thanks 2birds, that's what I needed to know!!<P>DCR_DAD||||reg||14
